{%- comment -%}
  Bassface breadcrumb — the "Home / Category / This Page" row.

  Accepts:
    current      - the current page's label. Required. Rendered as text, never a
                   link, and carries aria-current="page".
    parent_label - optional middle crumb. Omitted entirely when blank, which is
                   how a two-crumb trail is asked for.
    parent_url   - optional link for the middle crumb. With a label but no URL
                   the crumb renders as plain text, which is what a product type
                   with no matching collection needs.
    home_label   - defaults to 'Home'.
    label        - the landmark name read by screen readers. Defaults to
                   'Breadcrumb'.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'bf-breadcrumb', current: product.title, parent_label: 'Tees' -%}

  The consumer loads bf-breadcrumb.css.

  Three crumbs is the maximum by design, not by omission — every board draws
  exactly Home / Category / Page, and a variadic list in Liquid means passing
  parallel delimited strings that break on the first title containing the
  delimiter. Product titles here already contain commas, hyphens and brackets.

  The separators are <li aria-hidden> rather than CSS ::before content. A
  generated slash is not in the accessibility tree at all, so a screen reader
  reads the trail as one run-on string; an aria-hidden element is skipped by
  assistive tech but still separates the crumbs for everyone else, including
  when the row wraps.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign home_label = home_label | default: 'Home'
  assign label = label | default: 'Breadcrumb'
-%}

<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="{{ label }}">
  <ol class="breadcrumb__list">
    <li class="breadcrumb__item">
      <a class="breadcrumb__link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ home_label }}</a>
    </li>

    {%- if parent_label != blank -%}
      <li class="breadcrumb__item" aria-hidden="true">/</li>
      <li class="breadcrumb__item">
        {%- if parent_url != blank -%}
          <a class="breadcrumb__link" href="{{ parent_url }}">{{ parent_label }}</a>
        {%- else -%}
          {{ parent_label }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}

    <li class="breadcrumb__item" aria-hidden="true">/</li>
    <li class="breadcrumb__item breadcrumb__item--current" aria-current="page">{{ current }}</li>
  </ol>
</nav>
